\begin{align*}
10p + 2q &= 5.00 \quad \text{(3)} \\
5p + 10q &= 9.25 \quad \text{(4)}
\end{align*}
Subtracting equation (4) from equation (3) gives:
\begin{align*}
(10p + 2q) - (5p + 10q) &= 5.00 - 9.25 \\
5p - 8q &= -4.25 \\
p &= \frac{-4.25 + 8q}{5} \\
p &= 0.85 - \frac{8q}{5}
\end{align*}
Substituting this expression for $p$ into equation (2) gives:
\begin{align*}
(0.85 - \frac{8q}{5}) + 2q &= 1.85 \\
0.85 + \frac{2q}{5} &= 1.85 \\
\frac{2q}{5} &= 1 \\
q &= 2.50
\end{align*}
Substituting this value of $q$ back into equation (1) gives:
\begin{align*}
5p + 2.50 &= 2.50 \\
5p &= 0 \\
p &= 0
\end{align*}
Therefore, the cost of two pencils and one pen is $2(0.85 - \frac{8(2.50)}{5}) + 2.50 = \boxed{3.05}$.The answer is: 3.05

